# BlogWithCodes — project context

## Product
- Brand: **BlogWithCodes** (no spaces). Owner: Manish Bhatia (Senior Software Developer, India; trekker/traveller).
- Path: Angular portfolio + blog for GitHub Pages.
- Stack: Angular 22 standalone + lazy routes, Tailwind CSS v4.
- Host: GitHub Pages (`npm run build:ghpages`, base href `/BlogWithCodes_Portfolio-BlogSite/`).
- Theme: alpine blue + pine green; fonts Outfit + Source Sans 3; shared `app-icon`; brand logo in header/favicon under `public/assets/brand/`.

## Routes (do not invent new ones unless asked)
`/`, `/projects`, `/projects/:slug`, `/blog`, `/blog/category/:category`, `/blog/:slug`, `/places`, `/places/:slug`

## Landing shape (unchanged unless asked)
Hero → About → Working approach → Experience → Places preview → Blog preview → Contact  
Do **not** put projects back on the landing page.

## Content-driven architecture
- Site/profile: `public/content/site.json`
- Posts index + HTML: `public/content/posts/`
- Places: `public/content/places.json`
- Projects: `public/content/projects/index.json`
- Media: local only under `public/assets/…`; use `assetUrl` pipe for base-href-safe paths.
- Prefer extending existing services/components over new abstractions.

## Hard do-nots
- Do not invent brand name variants.
- Do not show end-user “edit JSON” copy on Places.
- Do not commit `Blogger/` Takeout (local source only; gitignored).
- Read existing files before changing; only change what the user asks.

## Contact / social source of truth
Update links in `public/content/site.json` (`social.*`, `email`, experience `companyUrl`). Do not hardcode URLs in templates when content already provides them.
